   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## controlnet-union.json\n\nControlNet-Union SDXL\n\nU6b - ControlNet-Union SDXL (xinsir, Apache-2.0 repack, 2.34 GB): ONE model for many modes via SetUnionControlNetType. GOTCHA (cost real debugging time): the `type` strings are GROUPED, not per-model - 'canny' is INVALID and the error is only in the server log: valid values are ['auto','openpose','depth','hed/pidi/scribble/ted','canny/lineart/anime_lineart/mlsd','normal','segment','tile','repaint']. Worse, ComfyUI reported status='success' while printing 'Output will be ignored' ONLY to the journal - a 3 s 'successful' run that produced no image. When a run succeeds suspiciously fast and saves nothing, check `journalctl --user -u comfyui`, not the API status. VERDICT: union/canny matched the specialist xinsir-canny-sdxl-v2 visually on the same seed (both restyled the cottage to a gothic mansion preserving roofline/dormers/chimney/door), and the same 2.34 GB file also did depth - replacing three specialist SD1.5 CNs plus the SDXL canny. NOTE: a raw edge-IoU metric said specialist 16% vs union 1.5%, but that was confounded by brightness (the union output is far darker, so a fixed gradient threshold finds fewer edges) - the images agree, the metric lied. To run depth instead, point SetUnionControlNetType at 'depth' and feed DepthAnythingV2Preprocessor.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S2** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **U6b** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  }
